    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0463" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg455"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/14808: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-07T11:00:00+03:25">September 7, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 8—5:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>140. With reference to my No. 138<anchor n="40" xml:id="d445-f1"/> the British
                    Minister has informed me of the following developments: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Because of Russian insistence the Bulgarians will be allowed to remain
                            in Iran;</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The Russians have refused the Iranian request for alteration of their
                            occupied zone but the British have approved the stationing of Iranian
                            troops in Dizful and Khorramabad;</item>
                        <pb facs="0464" n="456" xml:id="pg456"/>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>The Foreign Minister still urges a plan for the internment of Axis
                            nationals at Shiraz under British-Iranian control and at Meshed under
                            Russian-Iranian control. The British Minister has telegraphed this
                            proposal to London at the risk of further reprimand.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
